From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] photon: usr_lib_exec is /usr/libexec, as for the other RPM
 distros

Distro.usr_lib_exec defaults to /usr/lib in cloudinit/distros/__init__.py,
and photon.py does not override it - while rhel.py:30 sets /usr/libexec.

The meson install puts the helpers in libexecdir:

    /usr/libexec/cloud-init/write-ssh-key-fingerprints
    /usr/libexec/cloud-init/hook-hotplug

so cc_keys_to_console looks for write-ssh-key-fingerprints under
/usr/lib/cloud-init and does not find it. Distro.get_clouddir() derives
from the same attribute.

This is the same libexecdir-vs-lib mismatch the generator template has,
expressed in Python rather than in a rendered shell script. Upstream issue
6588 describes the class of bug.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 cloudinit/distros/photon.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/cloudinit/distros/photon.py
+++ b/cloudinit/distros/photon.py
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
     network_conf_dir = "/etc/systemd/network/"
     systemd_locale_conf_fn = "/etc/locale.conf"
     resolve_conf_fn = "/etc/systemd/resolved.conf"
+    usr_lib_exec = "/usr/libexec"
 
     renderer_configs = {
         "networkd": {
